s}_{0}+9.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b781ac41-d289-50fe-8eb5-284b3b53ff9b" :question/id #uuid "b781ac41-d289-50fe-8eb5-284b3b53ff9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-331765" :question/problem "Consider a function $h(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L\\{h(t)\\}=H(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{e}^{5t}h(t)\\}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{5t}h(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,h(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{5t}h(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{5t}\\,h(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-5)t}\\,h(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $H(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,h(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-5)t}\\,h(t)\\,\\text{d}t=H(s-5),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-5>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3120a6d5-36ac-5b9c-90c0-9b07c002842c" "answer-field-dceb88f7-92bd-5036-a0c6-c37c572187a4" "answer-field-b9b4b5af-a4ef-5c82-9e36-a78f516f5415" "answer-field-ac95803e-5be8-57a3-bc6d-baeb039e08ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3120a6d5-36ac-5b9c-90c0-9b07c002842c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3120a6d5-36ac-5b9c-90c0-9b07c002842c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-69368f31-eaf2-5e00-a00e-d2227104ef56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-50ed0ba1-3b5a-51d2-8abf-405c52c07533" "answer-69368f31-eaf2-5e00-a00e-d2227104ef56" "answer-82bbbbf3-e443-51c2-9f54-fc6a06cd84e9" "answer-06e0ebd2-9d85-5fa7-b531-e1c